Mechanical Design Toolkit: third-party boundaries

The top-level MIT license covers toolkit-authored code and documentation.
It does not relicense dependencies, model weights, host applications, browsers
or optional viewer assets.

Runtime dependencies are installed separately; their binaries and source
distributions are NOT included in this archive:

  Manifold3D: https://github.com/elalish/manifold
    Apache License 2.0; retain its distribution's LICENSE and notices.
  NumPy: https://numpy.org/
    BSD-3-Clause and additional bundled-component licenses. Use the complete
    notices supplied by the actual NumPy wheel, not just its primary license.
  Trimesh: https://github.com/mikedh/trimesh
    MIT; retain its distribution's copyright and license.

Optional browser validation uses separately installed Playwright
(https://github.com/microsoft/playwright, Apache-2.0) and a compatible browser.
Browser binaries and Playwright are not bundled. Browser terms are separate.

The default lightweight HTML viewer's toolkit code is included. The optional
embedded viewer runtime (including three-cad-viewer and its dependencies) is
NOT included. If supplied separately, retain its full notices and asset manifest;
the toolkit's MIT license does not replace them.

Copilot, OpenCode, Ollama, OpenAI clients and model weights are not bundled.
Users obtain them separately under their own licenses and service terms.
Local inference does not change model-license obligations.

When distributing generated projects containing copied cadkit source, include
the toolkit LICENSE and this notice alongside the project. The current starter
helper does not automatically copy these notices. Dependency redistribution
may carry additional obligations; preserve the notices in those distributions.
